        db 'BURN is only for a system that was uprooted (`uproot GO` first).', 10, 0
d_38ffa:
        db 'Burning: your objects are removed and written over with zeros ...', 10, 0
d_3903d:
        db 'Done. This machine is a fresh one: a new identity at the next start, no password.', 10
        db 'It restarts now.', 10, 0
d_390a1:
        db 'uprooting: this system goes onto a stick', 0
d_390ca:
        db 'UPROOTED: this system lives on the stick now', 0
d_390f7:
        db 'uprooting failed: nothing moved', 0
d_39117:
        db 'rooting down from the stick onto a disk', 0
d_3913f:
        db 'rooted here again: this one is the living system', 0
d_39170:
        db 'The chain: ', 0
d_3917c:
        db ' records kept (', 0
d_3918c:
        db ' written since the first). The last ones:', 10, 0
d_391b7:
        db 0x20, 0x20, 0x00
d_391ba:
        db 'Every record fits the one before it: the chain is unbroken.', 10, 0
d_391f7:
        db 'BROKEN: record ', 0
d_39207:
        db ' (of those kept) does not fit the one before it - a line was changed or removed.', 10, 0
d_39259:
        db 'This system was UPROOTED: it lives on from the stick (or where that was rooted).', 10
        db 'If the stick was lost: `root here` (maint) makes this one the living system again.', 10, 0
d_392fe:
        db 'uproot GO (maint) moves this system - the kernel, every object, the passwords, its identity', 10
        db 'and its key - onto the USB stick that is in. EVERYTHING on the stick is lost. Unlike', 10
        db '`puffer CLONE` the stick is not a child: it IS this machine. Start the other machine from', 10
        db 'it and type `root` there. This machine stays as it was, marked as uprooted.', 10, 0
d_39456:
        db 'This system runs from a stick: it is already uprooted - `root` puts it down on a disk.', 10, 0
d_394ae:
        db 'The stick was not written (see above): nothing moved, this is still the living system.', 10, 0
d_39506:
        db 0x0A
        db 'Uprooted. The stick is this machine now. Start the other machine from it and type `root`.', 10
        db 'This one is SEALED from now: no desktop, no programs. When the other machine runs:', 10
        db '`uproot BURN` here wipes it to a fresh system. If the stick is lost: `root here`.', 10, 0
d_39607:
        db '`root` is typed on the machine that was started from the uprooted stick.', 10
        db '(Here: `root here` says the stick was lost and this is the living system again.)', 10, 0
d_396a2:
        db 'root N ERASE  = this system down onto disk N, the whole disk (everything on it is lost)', 10
        db 'root N BESIDE = next to what is there. It stays the same machine: identity, key, objects.', 10, 0
d_39755:
        db 'If the lines above say it was written: take the stick out and start from the disk.', 10
        db 'Then the stick is a second copy of the same machine: keep it put away, or `puffer GO` over it.', 10, 0
d_39808:
        db 'This is the living system again.', 10, 0

